Re-gated docs/agents/test-specs/REQ-026.md (branch feature/WF02-REQ-026, commit c852e70) against the specific FAIL recorded in handoffs/WF02-REQ-026/step-03b-test-design-validator.json (AC8's false claim that this spec's non-doors-time-leak assertion 'closes a gap' in BACKEND-DEV's committed reminderJobs.db.test.ts AC8 case, when that case already asserts the same property at lines 479-487, not just the doorsLabel-absence check at line 477 that TEST-DESIGNER's original citation stopped at).

Read core-directives.md and WF-02 Step 3b. Diffed the rework: `git show c852e70 -- docs/agents/test-specs/REQ-026.md` and `git show --stat c852e70` (only docs/agents/test-specs/REQ-026.md plus TEST-DESIGNER's own handoffs/WF02-REQ-026/step-03-test-designer-rework1.json changed -- no other file touched).

Three corrected spots, all confirmed factually accurate:

1. Independence note's AC8 bullet (top of file): now states BACKEND-DEV's committed AC8 case already asserts 'neither non-doors item's own time leaks' at lines 479-487 ('confirmed by direct read'), and re-grounds this case's sole independent value as the different agenda-kind vocabulary ('workshop'/'afterparty' vs BACKEND-DEV's 'networking'/'close') proving kind === "doors" is a genuine equality check, not vocabulary-specific.

2. AC8 section's pass condition + failure-mode text: no longer claims 'this spec's version closes that gap' -- now states plainly that BACKEND-DEV's case already contains this exact assertion (lines 479-487) and this case does not close a gap there; its failure-mode paragraph now correctly targets a bug that matches on something other than a genuine kind === "doors" equality (e.g. a hardcoded blocklist of BACKEND-DEV's specific 'networking'/'close' strings, or a check keyed off string length/position/count) -- such a bug would still pass BACKEND-DEV's own case (whose specific strings it happens to reject) but fail this case's different vocabulary, which is the real, narrower thing this case proves.

3. Coverage table's AC8 row: now reads 'New case using a different agenda-kind vocabulary ("workshop"/"afterparty") than BACKEND-DEV's own AC8 case; re-runs the same "no doors label, no non-doors item's own time" assertion shape BACKEND-DEV's case already has, independently confirming kind === "doors" is a real equality check rather than vocabulary-specific' -- no residual gap-closure claim.

Independently re-read apps/bot/src/scheduler/reminderJobs.db.test.ts lines 460-488 myself (not trusting the citation): confirmed lines 476-487 read
```
    expect(message.caption).not.toContain(catalog.reminder3h.doorsLabel);
    expect(message.caption).toContain(startsText);
    // Neither non-doors agenda item's own time ever leaks into the caption
    // (unless it happens to coincide with startsText, which these fixture
    // times do not).
    if (networkingText !== startsText) {
      expect(message.caption).not.toContain(networkingText);
    }
    if (closingText !== startsText) {
      expect(message.caption).not.toContain(closingText);
    }
```
The non-doors-time-leak assertion (networkingText/closingText absence) is indeed present at lines 479-487 in the committed test, exactly as the corrected spec now states. The citation is accurate.

Confirmed the AC8 test case's own mechanics in the spec (fixture: fresh event with 'workshop'/'afterparty' agenda-kind items, own timestamps; assertions: absence of doors label AND absence of both non-doors items' own formatted times) are byte-for-byte unchanged from the prior (FAILed) version -- only the surrounding justification/claim text was corrected, not the case itself, matching the task's expected rework shape.

Confirmed nothing else in the spec was touched: `git show c852e70 --stat` shows a single file changed (docs/agents/test-specs/REQ-026.md, 41 insertions/15 deletions all within the three AC8-related spots) plus TEST-DESIGNER's own handoff record; all other ACs (1-10), the forged-callback section, and the rest of the coverage table are untouched from the version whose other checks already PASSed in the prior gate run (AC7 substring extraction, AC3 two-process construction, forged-callback variant coverage, real grammY dispatch, no TODOs, per-AC case coverage/precision) and do not need re-examination since no other content changed.

No 'TODO' found (grep -in TODO: zero matches, consistent with the prior gate's finding on an unchanged rest-of-file). Every AC still has at least one precise, mechanically-runnable verification case naming exact commands/fixtures/expected values. The false factual claim that caused the original FAIL is gone and the case's real, narrower justification is now accurately stated. PASS.
